 "answer_text": "Found 5 pubmed records, 1 medgen record, 5 clinical trial records and 1 literature entity record for Marfan syndrome [13][14][15][16][17][18][19][79][80][81][82][83]. \n\nMarfan syndrome phenotype\n\nThere is currently no radical treatment, but early identification, diagnosis, and treatment can prolong patient life span [1]. \n\nClinical features from MedGen\n\nMedGen lists these clinical features: Aortic regurgitation [2], Arachnodactyly [3], Astigmatism [4], Ectopia lentis [5], Esotropia [6], Exotropia [7], Pes planus [8], Glaucoma [9], Congestive heart failure [10], Hypertropia [11] and Micrognathia [12]. \n\nAngiotensin Converting Enzyme Inhibitors in Marfan Syndrome [13], Marfan syndrome [14], Losartan Versus Atenolol for the Treatment of Marfan Syndrome [15], Marfan syndrome [16] and A Randomized, Open-label, LOSARTAN Therapy on the Progression of Aortic Root Dilation in Patients With Marfan Syndrome [17]. \n\nPubmed records found\n\nPubmed title: Marfan syndrome [18]. Pubmed title: [Latest advances in the diagnosis and treatment of Marfan syndrome] [81]. Pubmed title: What Is Marfan Syndrome [83]. Pubmed title: Marfan syndrome [14]. Pubmed title: Marfan syndrome [16]. \n\nMedgen records found\n\nMedgen title: Marfan syndrome [19]. \n\nClinical features MedGen lists for Marfan syndrome\n\nMedgen clinical_features: Aortic regurgitation [2]. Medgen clinical_features: Arachnodactyly [3]. Medgen clinical_features: Astigmatism [4]. Medgen clinical_features: Ectopia lentis [5]. Medgen clinical_features: Esotropia [6]. Medgen clinical_features: Exotropia [7]. Medgen clinical_features: Pes planus [8]. Medgen clinical_features: Glaucoma [9]. Medgen clinical_features: Congestive heart failure [10]. Medgen clinical_features: Hypertropia [11]. Medgen clinical_features: Micrognathia [12]. Medgen clinical_features: Mitral regurgitation [20]. Medgen clinical_features: Mitral valve prolapse [21]. Medgen clinical_features: Myopia [22]. Medgen clinical_features