es: Mitral annular calcification [63]. Medgen clinical_features: Long face [64]. Medgen clinical_features: Disproportionate tall stature [65]. Medgen clinical_features: Decreased muscle mass [66]. Medgen clinical_features: Narrow face [67]. Medgen clinical_features: Dural ectasia [68]. Medgen clinical_features: Reduced subcutaneous adipose tissue [69]. Medgen clinical_features: Malar flattening [70]. Medgen clinical_features: Equinus calcaneus [71]. Medgen clinical_features: Joint hypermobility [72]. Medgen clinical_features: Limited elbow extension [73]. Medgen clinical_features: Pectus excavatum [74]. Medgen clinical_features: Medial rotation of the medial malleolus [75]. Medgen clinical_features: Spontaneous cerebrospinal fluid leak [76]. Medgen clinical_features: Metatarsus adductus [77]. Medgen clinical_features: Reduced upper to lower segment ratio [78]. \n\nLiterature entity records found\n\nLiterature entity name: Marfan Syndrome [79]. \n\nClinical trial records found\n\nClinical trial name: Studies of Heritable Disorders of Connective Tissue [80]. Clinical trial name: Comparison of Two Medications Aimed at Slowing Aortic Root Enlargement in Individuals With Marfan Syndrome [82]. Clinical trial name: Angiotensin Converting Enzyme Inhibitors in Marfan Syndrome [13]. Clinical trial name: Losartan Versus Atenolol for the Treatment of Marfan Syndrome [15]. Clinical trial name: A Randomized, Open-label, LOSARTAN Therapy on the Progression of Aortic Root Dilation in Patients With Marfan Syndrome [17]. "
